ict, covering steps pick_u_brown, place_approach_u_brown, place_u_brown, reseat_u_brown, pick_u_orange, transport_and_approach_place_u_orange, place_u_orange, pick_line_green, reorient_and_place_approach_line_green, place_line_green, pick_inverted_u_yellow, place_approach_inverted_u_yellow, place_inverted_u_yellow. Three of these (reseat_u_brown, transport_and_approach_place_u_orange, reorient_and_place_approach_line_green) were not on the expected process map; each violated nothing I had standing at the time, so each is a valid, unflagged variation in its own right, named here as unplanned per the recording requirement.\n\nOne finding was recorded during the run: at place_u_brown's close, my own query_snapshot measurement (0.01306 m position error against the 0.01 m position tolerance, 27.8 deg orientation error against the 10 deg bound, both independently matching the executor's own claim_detail) showed u_brown mis-seated, consistent with the part catching or tipping against the fixture during descent rather than landing flush; this was recorded non_conformant under step_id place_u_brown. The executor then ran an unplanned reseat_u_brown: re-grasped u_brown (slip monitor re-armed and never fired), lifted, re-approached with extra standoff and a slower descent, and released. I independently measured the result at reseat_u_brown's close: u_brown at (0.39737,-0.13919,0.04369) against placement (0.39858,-0.13950,0.04538), a 0.0021 m error, well inside the 0.01 m tolerance -- a genuine recovery, not merely a repeated claim.\n\nAt run end I independently queried every part and its placement frame rather than relying on the executor's run_ended status or its per-step claim_detail: u_brown 0.00237 m (tol 0.01), u_orange 0.00212 m (tol 0.02), line_green 0.00653 m (tol 0.015), inverted_u_yellow 0.00153 m (tol 0.012) -- all comfortably inside their respective raw_spec.tolerances.position_m bounds, with orientation likewise aligned in each case. The clamp-effort invariant (invariants.grasp_effort_instantaneous) held throughout every pick/place for every part -- peaks of ~60 (u_brown), ~58 (u_orange reseat), and ~78 (inverted_u_yellow) sim_effort, all far under their respective max_clamp_effort bounds of 100/200/170/250 -- and no slip monitor fired on any held part before its intentional release, so neither the clamp nor in-hand-slippage invariants were ever in question.\n\nbase1 (the fixture) and all four bystanders (u_green, inverted_u_brown, hex_blue, hex_red, base2) were monitored by stationarity for the entire run from before the first step. None of their monitors fired. At run end I re-measured each against its run-start reference: the bystanders moved essentially not at all (<0.0002 m each), and base1 moved 0.01317 m from its run-start position -- below the 0.02 m bound I used, but that bound is agent-chosen (get_contract has no entry for base1, since it is never named by any step, so no contract-backed disturbance tolerance exists for it; I reused the 0.02 m disturbance_tolerance_m value common to every FMB part contract in this registry as the best available analogue). I flag this explicitly rather than silently treating it as a zero-risk pass: base1's measured drift is real and plausibly reflects light contact from a carried part's approach error (most likely during the u_brown mis-seat/reseat sequence, which happened at the adjacent placement site), but it stayed under the threshold I applied, so it does not constitute a standing violation under the only tolerance available to judge it by.\n\nWith every part's final pose within tolerance, the clamp and slippage invariants holding throughout, and no bystander or fixture disturbance exceeding its (contract-backed or, for base1, agent-chosen) bound, the run's end-state is conformant. The one mid-run non-conformance (place_u_brown) was corrected before the run ended, which is why this is a recovery rather than a clean run.","run_scope":true,"executor_terminal_status":"completed","findings_during_run":["place_u_brown"],"recovered":true},"subscriber_count":2,"seq":55}
